      "text": "Strategy-drift monitoring compares deployed decisions and behavior against research or shadow expectations while investigating execution-mode differences. The evidence covers parallel out-of-sample reconciliation, operational state checks, per-pair model freshness, replay-based diagnosis, lookahead checks, and historical mismatch reports. Divergence needs attribution before it is treated as signal decay: data history, prediction reloads, timing, and simulation behavior can differ. Monitoring and pause suggestions are distinguished from validated thresholds, and an internal documentation conflict over expiry configuration remains unresolved.",
